**Approach**
Observe that there is always an even number of piles.
Alice can decide to collect either all even-indexed piles or all odd-indexed piles.
Since the total number of stones is odd, one parity must have a strictly larger sum.
Alice chooses that parity and can always force the game to follow that strategy.
Hence, the answer is always true.
